    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve never though about that, but in the actual script the calls are identically formatted. T<span style=\"font-size:13px\">he problem still occurs when age is exchanged with (any) other variable, for example a dummy coded sex-variable. </span><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Don&#39;t know if following information helps, but the problem does not occur when delta-parameterization is used instead of theta.</span><br></div><div><div><div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br></span></div></div></div></div>"
